fin-portfolio:FXConversionShape a sh:NodeShape;
    sh:description "FX Conversion, is an auditable fact that applies an exact PIT FX rate and direction to convert one Money into another (a rate application, also referenced as FXRateApplication), used for being uniquely consumed by a valuation line, opening lot, or fee allocation that points back to this exact conversion version. Optional rateSource, quoteTime, rateDate, rateFinality, and crossRatePath carry the rate provenance and multi-leg cross-currency path. If this fact represents a real FX trade rather than a rate application, it belongs to trading or settlement semantics and should reference a settlement/trading module fact.";
    sh:name "FX Conversion";
