fin-portfolio:PositionSnapshotShape a sh:NodeShape;
    sh:description "Position Snapshot, is a signed exposure observation of one account and instrument from a single observation stream, used for storing the signed net quantity as the default directional truth where positive is long, negative is short, zero is flat, and any side label is derived. Optional grossLongQuantity, grossShortQuantity, positionScope, and balanceDimension carry the gross and per-bucket truths so that the signed net is no longer the only authoritative quantity.";
    sh:name "Position Snapshot";
